/T (1. Hedging in Crypto Trading Hedging is a risk management strategy used to offset potential losses in one position by taking an opposite position in a related asset. In crypto trading, hedging can help protect your portfolio from market volatility and reduce the impact of sudden price swings.)
/E (1. Hedging in Crypto Trading Hedging is a risk management strategy used to offset potential losses in one position by taking an opposite position in a related asset. In crypto trading, hedging can help protect your portfolio from market volatility and reduce the impact of sudden price swings.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 143 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
2412 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 4224 0 R
/E (How Hedging Works: In a typical hedge, you might hold a long position in a cryptocurrency while simultaneously taking a short position in the same or a correlated asset. If the price of the cryptocurrency drops, the short position gains, offsetting the loss from the long position.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 143 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2413 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 4225 0 R
/E (Hedging with Derivatives: One of the most common ways to hedge in crypto trading is through derivatives such as futures contracts or options. For example, if you hold a significant amount of Bitcoin and want to hedge against potential downside risk, you can short Bitcoin futures contracts or buy Bitcoin put options, which increase in value if the price of Bitcoin falls.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 143 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2414 0 obj
