/E (Use Stop-Loss and Take-Profit Orders: Using stop-loss and take-profit orders helps remove emotional decision-making from the equation. A stop-loss order automatically closes your position when the price drops to a certain level, limiting your losses. A take-profit order does the opposite, locking in profits when the price hits a predetermined target. These tools help you stick to your strategy, even in the face of market fluctuations.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 168 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2531 0 obj
<<
