/T (1. Leverage and Margin Trading Leverage allows traders to control a larger position with a smaller amount of capital, magnifying both potential profits and potential losses. In margin trading, you borrow funds from a broker or exchange to increase your trade size. What is Leverage? Leverage is the ability to borrow capital to trade larger positions than your account balance would normally allow. For example, with 10x leverage, you can control a position worth $10,000 with just $1,000 of your own capital.)
